{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"RESULT: FINDINGS\n\nI read `site/v2/one/login.tsx`, `card.tsx`, `deck/data.ts`, `deck/marks.tsx` and the six images in order. The form is locked and neat. The right side is not.\n\n1. Why Center Flow failed, in his words\n\nEffect itself: \"absolutely hate the effect this center flow produces. Despise it.\" The blue pulses and glow around the card read as catalog motion pasted on.\nFrame: a tech demo object next to a product. His rejection rule for wires holds here: \"Logically, those elements don't go together over there\" and \"the flowchart feeding into the story, that thing. That's so stupid.\"\nObjects: a diagram of sources is not the product. His rule from the council: when he names a real object, that object goes in the frame. Generic Globe and Rss glyphs plus lines stand in for real cards, real pictures and real marks.\n\n2. The right side: two options, ranked\n\nOption 1, first. A small piece of the feed itself.\nLine 1, objects: four real `StoryCard` cards with their real pictures and marks: Olmo-core 3, MAI, Mistral in Germany, Latent Space photo.\nLine 2, arrangement: a compact two by two grid right of the 420px form, top aligned with the form, same DESIGN.md skin and shadows.\nLine 3, motion: nothing moves. No pulses, no orbit, no scroll.\nLine 4, reads as what you get: this is your feed after login, readable on arrival with headlines and two facts each.\nLine 5, must not become: not a fan that competes with the form, not a dimmed backdrop, not a catalog block.\n\nOption 2, second. One story, fully readable.\nLine 1, objects: one large `StoryCard` for the GPT-6.1 Sol story with its Latent Space picture and its real source marks.\nLine 2, arrangement: one card right of the 420px form, same width family as the form, centered vertically.\nLine 3, motion: nothing moves.\nLine 4, reads as what you get: one story made from many reports, the product job in one object.\nLine 5, 